            <ArticleTitle>[Minimally invasive surgical approach for the low back pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The fact that minimally invasive surgery for the low back pain is considerably less traumatic has been documented by two broad categories consisted of intradiscal therapeutic and endoscopic procedures. A marked reduction in length of hospitalization has been noted in many cases. Surgeons should select the procedure, or combination of procedures, best suited to benefit of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
